sions Visit Meet an Admissions Counselor Accepted Students Support & Career Center for Academic Excellence Internships Only at Alverno Research Center for Women and Girls Thea Bowman Institute for Excellence and Leadership Registration Office of the Registrar Register for Classes Catalogs & Policies Campus Visit Us About Alverno About A Hispanic-Serving Institution First-Generation College Students Where All Belong Alverno's President Campus Events Campus Life Residence Life Dining Services Student Activities Greenhouse Campus Ministry Campus Safety Store A-Store (Alverno Gear) Resources Academic Academic Advising Career Studio Instructional Services Library Student Development and Success Study Abroad Technology Media Hub Tech Services Registration Office of the Registrar Register for Classes Accounts Student Accounts Financial Aid Health & Safety Wellness Campus Safety Additional Resources Resources for Parents All Student Resources Internal Event Brand Guide Alverno Publications 8 Abilities 8 Abilities Center for Learning and Assessment Support Volunteer Assessor Program Assessment Workshops & Consulting Alverno News Faculty Experts News/Blog A Magazine Apply Request Info Athletics Visit Events Alumnae Give My Alverno Career Studio Career Resources Student Resources Career Coaching Internship Advising Internship Advising Forms Recent Internships Handshake Alum Resources Handshake Employer Resources Hire an Intern Recruit a Grad Handshake Internship Forms Community Resources Online Resources Career Studio Team Office Hours & Contact Info Welcome to Alverno’s Career Studio Alverno’s Career Studio is a creative space where students become the artists of their future. Students are empowered to express individual ideas and collective imagination. It is the\n        place where goals and dreams originate through career exploration, professional development, and internship experiences. Read more from our students on what it is like to intern in our community Schedule an appointment with a Career Coach today! Appointments To schedule an appointment with a Career Coach during regular office hours ,\n        log into Handshake . The Virtual Interview Room is available for student use by appointment. Please use Handshake to\n        reserve a time (select appointment ). Students may shop the Career Studio Boutique during our office\n        hours . Walk-ins For quick questions, stop in during our office hours . For everything else, please\n        schedule an appointment in Handshake . News You Can Use Alverno's Career Studio is home to an Iris Booth , one of only 35 educational institutions in the country to provide this technology to students. Read more . Kohl’s has committed to provide five $5,000 merit-based scholarships to support Alverno students, with a special focus on supporting women of color and/or are the first\n        in their families to attend college. Read more . Learn about our Kohl's Scholars . General Inquiries For general inquiries, please reach out via email to careerstudio@alverno.edu . Mannequins with meaning The Career Studio team have been striving to create a space that engages students in not only career aspirations but personal growth. Recently, they revealed the arrival of a new mannequin to join another — known on campus as Ali Schall. The newest mannequin, provided by Kohl's, has a visible scar on her hand \"to\n        represent every story, every setback, every struggle, every pain and every success of an Alverno College Strong Woman.\" Career Studio staff have been working  to expand representation of our Beloved Alverno community by showcasing fashion mannequins of different sizes, shapes, and skin tones. The Career Boutique invites students to prepare themselves professionally and personally, offering free clothing as they grow during their Alverno journey. Interested in donating to the Career Boutique? Donation guidelines Thank you for your consideration of a donation to the Alverno Career Boutique. We are seeking: New or gently used clothing in the business casual to business professional range women, men and gender neutral. Any and all sizes and seasons of adult clothing and accessories are appreciated, including maternity items. All items should be cleaned prior to donation with no rips, stains, broken zippers, or other imperfections. Clothes should be good to excellent quality and purchased within the last five\n        years/current with fashion. We are currently accepting donations on Mondays from 9 a.m. – noon and Wednesdays from 1 – 3 p.m. Desired items Dresses Blazers / cardigans Blouses / dress shirts / sweaters Skirts Dress slacks / khakis Hosiery / tights / leggings Shoes Jewelry / belts / accessories Handbags Messenger bags / laptop bags Coats, hats, gloves, cold weather scarves Scarves Men's clothing Gender neutral clothing Follow us on Facebook Follow us on Instagram Ready for what's next Request More Info Apply Now Explore Programs 3400 S. 43rd St. Milwaukee, WI 53219 414-382-6000 admissions@alverno.edu Campus Map Mesa Location Contact Us Employment at Alverno Event Spaces Faculty Directory Trustees Privacy Policy Faculty & Staff Intranet Accreditation Harassment/Discrimination Policy Web Accessibility Statement Institutional Review Board © Alverno College, All Rights Reserved"
    },
